# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the prefill SDPA programme's oneq jobs (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a
# throwaway commit of the integration branch (a branch that carries optimisation/ttnn-op/sdpa_prefill_oneq) and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. ONE TAG AT A TIME; wait for the run to
# finish; never cancel a running card job. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. A placeholder in @...@ is filled in by whoever drives the
# window (@SERVED_IMAGE@: the served image's reference; @K64J_OQ_GRAFT_DIR@ and @K64J_OQ_TTNNCPP_SHA256@: the K64j-OQ graft directory and its binary's digest, the K64J_OQ_TTNNCPP_SHA256 line of
# L1). C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the window's own image (sed -i 's/tp4-fusion-1/<tag>/' *.env). ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the read rules and the minutes.
# W1 (the first hardware pass of the oneq program, card M alone, after L1): run_card_m_oq.sh with WATCHER=1 - TT_METAL_WATCHER=5 (NoC sanitiser, waypoints, asserts) over the served shape in the arms
# stock / served (0x5EFA0003) / oneq (0x5EFA000B) / oneq_noc (0x5EFA000F), rows 2048 and 1024, five starts (0, 128, 2048, 65536, 251904), one seed, DRAM Q, no timing, plus the program-cache check and the
# refusals (TT_FATAL, never a hang). Every arm's bytes must equal the stock path's; the factory log must show 'flags=0xb kv_chain=1 chains=16 members=96' and the 'oneq=1 q_chunks=96 cores=<130 or 110>
# chunks_per_core=1' line for the 2048-row programs. The device grid is read from the card (13x10 since the firmware unlock) and reported.
# READ: 'ONEQ_CARD_M verdict=PASS ...' (exit 0) and 'watcher log ...: 0 error/assert lines'. A hang (the WATCHDOG line, exit 3) prints the reset hint for card M and card A TOGETHER; reset them, then a passing
# stock smoke run, before anything else. STOP rule: a FAIL, a watcher error or a hang stops the oneq program here (the chain protocol itself is unchanged: the receivers and the injector run the
# very reader that Q1 qualified, only the grouping differs). Duration (estimate): 40 min (container timeout 45 min; the first call of each program JIT-compiles it).
C2_CARDS=pair
C2_ACTIONS=cardm
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-1
C2_CARDM_HARNESS=optimisation/ttnn-op/sdpa_prefill_oneq/run_card_m_oq.sh
C2_CARDM_ARGS=
C2_CARDM_ENV=WATCHER=1 IMAGE=@SERVED_IMAGE@ KOPGRAFT64=@K64J_OQ_GRAFT_DIR@ EXPECT_TTNNCPP_SHA256=@K64J_OQ_TTNNCPP_SHA256@
